{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476937-time-travel-to-wipe-out-the-technocracy","id":1476937,"title":"Time travel to wipe out the Technocracy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-22T02:39:32-07:00","id":1476937,"title":"Time travel to wipe out the Technocracy","content":"I have long since fancied a rules and setting hack that lets the Ascension War turn Hot and engulf the other supernaturals as the Technocracy overreaches to expand and intensify the Pogrom, either out of its own hubris or from the covert instigation of Threat Null. Most Night-Folk reorganize into Triatic uber-factions that war for reality. A Technocracy civil war occurs between corrupted and uncorrupted factions that folds into the larger conflict. Consensus becomes accepting of low-key sci-fi, fantasy, and horror stuff. Banality and the Gauntlet considerably weaken and Tradition mages, shapeshifters, and changelings experience a major resurgence and population boost. The world becomes a war-torn science fantasy setting on the brink of Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> This setting change further enables my preferred rule hacks of no Vulgar Without Witnesses, rolling Arete + Sphere for magick, lethal soak for all supernaturals, no Avatar Storm, no or greatly weakened Acclimation or Disembodiment, etc. but they would exist even without the Reality War. The Consensus never became strong to weaken magick casting or cause Paradox in most cases without the active and present support of Sleeper disbelief or the mage bungling the spell. Awakening or getting a fae soul strengthens the body as much as being a vampire or shapeshifter, if in a different way. The Avatar Storm never existed, its destructive effects get partially replaced by the Reality War without restricting access to the Umbra.<br /> <br /> In this context, I got the idea to apply a classic sci-fi trope, time travel to change the past. A radical group of Tradition mages in the Dynamic faction gets desperate because they fear the Entropy faction may win (or theoretically the Stasis one, but they are the weakest side) or the war itself may destroy the world. They decide to travel to the past and prevent the rise of the Technocracy in the first place. They somehow harness the massive amount of Quintessence that is likely necessary to nullify the mind-boggling amount of Paradox that rewriting a millennium or so of history would cause. Therefore, Paradox cannot stop them. They are aware the timeline change would likely prevent the Council of Traditions and the technological and social benefits of modernity (unless mystical equivalents arise) from existing, but deem it an acceptable sacrifice to save the world. They could not care less if it means mages and other supernaturals get to keep lording it over humans as feudal masters, since they deem covert rule by the Technocracy and the Camarilla has been just as bad and it is still way better than the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Which would be the best focal point to prevent the Technocracy from existing? I have singled out two, and possibly another couple. The obvious possiblities seem intervening at Mistridge in 1210 to cause the defeat of the Craftmasons (which in all likelihood would cause the faction to be crushed or disband) or bomb the 997 Gathering of the Square that set up the Craftmasons and their nascent alliance with other proto-Order of Reason groups in the first place. Without the Craftmasons, chances are the proto-Technocracy never gets organized. A third obvious possibility is to destroy the Convention of the White Tower in 1325, although I am concerned by then the nascent Order of Reason had already got too momentum by then for its rise to be disrupted. Another possibility IMO is to kill the Tremere leaders in ca. 1000 when they turn themselves into vampires. Without the major distraction of the First Massassa War, chances are the Hermetics are able to nip the Craftmasons in the bud before they get too much momentum. Which do you think would be the best option?<br /> <br /> I suppose messing with the timeline this way is going to have major repercussions. Since Paradox has been defanged through massive Quintessence expenditure, I suppose we may expect rival time-travelers from the Static and/or Entropic factions to try and undo the change, or possibly even tinker with the timeline to their benefit (e.g. to prevent the Council of the Traditions and/or the Changeling Way from existing). The Reality War may well acquire a temporal frontline. Your ideas on this?<br /> <br /> In the case the Tradition/Dynamic radicals get successful, which kind of future are they going to create with no Technocracy? Broadly speaking, they are sincere in their commitment to save the world (even if they put the welfare of Tradition mages and other Dynamic supernaturals before the one of Sleepers) and their concerns are not without merit, although their fears might be exaggerated. Speaking from the ST perspective of an omniscient observer, the simplest and most effective solution to prevent an Entropic victory or too much damage to the world (a certain degree is likely unavoidable) may be a truce and alliance of convenience between the Dynamic and Static factions to fight the Entropics and set up a science fantasy Consensus, but this is far from simple or bound to occur.<br /> <br /> As it concerns the way time is going to work in this context, I waver between malleable time (think Back to the Future) or time travel causing alternate timelines (think Avengers: Endgame). Your suggestion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-22-2022, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T03:11:42-07:00","id":1476940,"title":"","content":"One difficulty for a time traveler is that the changes you've outlined for how Magick works <i>now</i> aren't going to apply <i>then</i>. Consider a more modest trip to explain this: a 20-year jump from 2022 to 2002. When your time traveling makes arrive, they're going to find themselves in a reality in magickal turmoil, where not only is Paradox not <i>weaker</i>, it's coming down like a <i>sledgehammer</i>: the MRev-era Paradox mechanics are in full effect. <br /> <br /> Travel back to the time of the Craftmasons' assault on Mistridge, and you'll find that the nature of magick will be even more different; one might even say alien to the time travelers. Their very presence is likely to be an ongoing \u201cParadox\u201d effect (though back then, it behaved very differently). Even if they themselves aren't being rejected by reality, their Magicks likely <i>will</i> be: it would bea good way for them to discover that their supposedly authentic magickal beliefs aren't really as authentic as they thought, and Effects that they take for granted as being Coincidental will turn out to be Vulgar (even without Witnesses, because this is a time period <i>before</i> \u201cVulgar without Witnesses\u201d ceased to be a thing). <br /> <br /> On the other hand, it's possible that the time travelers bring a bubble of modern-day reality with them to the Dark Ages, allowing them to continue to use their Magicks in the way that they're used to. <b>Mage</b> even had support for such a concept in its existing material: Marauders. <br /> <br /> My inclination would be to go with an Everett Volume, where by default changes to the past tend to cause an alternate timeline. That said, I could see Time mastery being used to set up an ongoing Effect that works against that, and attempts to integrate the changes made into the original timeline. The more drastic the change, the more likely it is to disrupt the Effect, spawning an Everett Volume in a manner not unlike a Paradox Realm and trapping the time travelers in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T03:24:32-07:00","id":1476942,"title":"","content":"I see your point, although I forgot to mention that I like the idea of No Vulgar w/o Witnesses (and rolling Arete + Sphere for magic) so much (and I hate pretty much all the other rules that enable the MRev metaplot and its preferential playstyle, such as the Avatar Storm, Acclimation/Disembodiment, No Lethal Soak, etc.) that I am entirely willing to change the system and setting accordingly in all eras.<br /> <br /> As far as I am concerned, the Reality War event further enables more permissive changes to the Consensus (e.g. low-key sci-fi and fantasy stuff becomes acceptable, Banality weakens, the Gauntlet weakens, etc.) but is not a necessary premise to remove Vulgar w/o Witnesses or enable more powerful magick casting. Vw/oW never existed (and the magick roll stayed Arete + Sphere as in DA:M and M:tSC) because the Consensus never got strong enough to enforce Paradox without the support of active and present Sleeper disbelief or the mage bungling the spell, or weaken magick casting. Broadly speaking, the Reality War may be a good replacement for the other destructive changes the MRev metaplot caused (e.g. a few Realms explode), without unduly restricting access to the Umbra, quite the contrary. Sorry for the misunderstanding, I hope the clarification helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-22-2022, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T04:51:21-07:00","id":1476946,"title":"","content":"You do you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T05:48:19-07:00","id":1476950,"title":"","content":"The main issue I see is a temporal paradox - they prevent the Technocracy from forming, there for there is no need for the action to prevent the Technocracy from forming. Thus it comes to a zero sum game, of if they do it, then they never did it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T08:55:39-07:00","id":1476967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>babi_gog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476937-time-travel-to-wipe-out-the-technocracy?p=1476950#post1476950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main issue I see is a temporal paradox - they prevent the Technocracy from forming, there for there is no need for the action to prevent the Technocracy from forming. Thus it comes to a zero sum game, of if they do it, then they never did it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You have a point. However, if we use the alternate-timelines model of time travel, this kind of temporal paradox typically gets nullified. The get to save a world (by their definition), just not the one they started from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-22-2022, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T10:29:50-07:00","id":1476979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476937-time-travel-to-wipe-out-the-technocracy#post1476937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are aware the timeline change would likely prevent the Council of Traditions and the technological and social benefits of modernity (unless mystical equivalents arise) from existing, but deem it an acceptable sacrifice to save the world. They could not care less if it means mages and other supernaturals get to keep lording it over humans as feudal masters, since they deem covert rule by the Technocracy and the Camarilla has been just as bad and it is still way better than the Apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my first posts was about<b></b>: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Population growth in mystic paradigm parallel world</span></span></a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T11:29:07-07:00","id":1476988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476937-time-travel-to-wipe-out-the-technocracy?p=1476967#post1476967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You have a point. However, if we use the alternate-timelines model of time travel, this kind of temporal paradox typically gets nullified. The get to save a world (by their definition), just not the one they started from.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the reasons I suggested what I did was that it gives the option of saving the one that you started from, given sufficient creativity; but even if you fail at that, you can <i>still</i> save <i>a</i> world. <br /> <br /> Assuming, of course, that you don't screw it up in other ways in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T13:42:25-07:00","id":1477011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476937-time-travel-to-wipe-out-the-technocracy?p=1476988#post1476988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the reasons I suggested what I did was that it gives the option of saving the one that you started from, given sufficient creativity; but even if you fail at that, you can <i>still</i> save <i>a</i> world.<br /> <br /> Assuming, of course, that you don't screw it up in other ways in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476937-time-travel-to-wipe-out-the-technocracy?p=1476940#post1476940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My inclination would be to go with an Everett Volume, where by default changes to the past tend to cause an alternate timeline. That said, I could see Time mastery being used to set up an ongoing Effect that works against that, and attempts to integrate the changes made into the original timeline. The more drastic the change, the more likely it is to disrupt the Effect, spawning an Everett Volume in a manner not unlike a Paradox Realm and trapping the time travelers in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. I suppose you are speaking about your Everett Volume idea. I am not familiar with the physics of the concept, but I suppose I broadly get the idea due to the apparent reference to the multiverse interpretation of quantum mechanics. Basically speaking, it means copy-and-paste superposing a new timeline created by time travel on the original one. The notion seems very interesting since it may work as a (double) backup plan. Broadly speaking, there is going to be Plan A): achieve a truce, an alliance of convenience, and a compromise deal for a syncretic science fantasy Consensus (kinda like your vanilla kitchen-sink comic-book universe) between the Dynamic and Static factions in the present. If that does not work and trying to win the Reality War w/o too much damage seems too difficult for the Dynamic faction alone, there is Plan B): change the past and copy-and-paste the new timeline on the original one with the Everett Volume effect. And if that fails or seems too difficult, there is Plan C): using the new timeline as a haven for refugees from the original timeline.<br /> <br /> By the way, I am already assuming the time travel effect is going to require truckloads of Quintessence to defuse Paradox since the timeline change is global, rewrites 700-1000 years of history (depending on the temporal flashpoint used), and massively changes the Consensus, the status of humanity, and the fate of most supernatural splats (most notably the mages, shapeshifters, and fae) and their Umbrood allies. The actors might get a little slack since they come from an Apocalyptic temporal flashpoint.where the Consensus is being shaked to the core and the Tellurian faces the very real possibility of the End Times if the Entropics get their way or the war escalates too much. I suppose the Everett Volume effect is going to take just as much effort in terms of successes and mystical juice since it has a similar impact. Although the time travel one in all likelihood is not going to require as many successes, since a good portion of its effectiveness comes from precisely targeting the intended timeline change. I am reminded of similar feats in the Ascension and Apocalypse books. But then again, that is the nature of the beast. The Reality War setting hack is supposed to be one big crossover-friendly Ascension/Apocalypse/Time of Judgement scenario stretched out to be the basis for a whole chronicle and replace the cloak-and-dagger canon setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-22-2022, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T13:56:01-07:00","id":1477012,"title":"","content":"\u201cEverett Volume\u201d is actually a Mage term, though it's borrowed from physics (the Everett-Wheeler Many Worlds interpretation of Quantum Physics, which posits a branching timeline at every decision point).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T14:07:56-07:00","id":1477018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476937-time-travel-to-wipe-out-the-technocracy?p=1477012#post1477012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cEverett Volume\u201d is actually a Mage term, though it's borrowed from physics (the Everett-Wheeler Many Worlds interpretation of Quantum Physics, which posits a branching timeline at every decision point).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, I see. I found the reference. I had failed to notice it since I typically pay very little attention to Technocracy stuff except as it concerns how to fight them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-22-2022, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T14:21:46-07:00","id":1477020,"title":"","content":"Yeah; well, that's the problem with assuming that the Technocracy has nothing worthwhile to contribute. For all of their copious faults, they are the premier champions of Science. And as such, you're going to find many concepts (ones rooted in Science) only in the Technocracy sections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http: